    id: "econ-2024-ol-sa-q10", topicId: "economics-1-0", conceptId: "which-diagram-shows-the-new-matcha-equilibrium",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2024 OL Section A Q10",
    stem: "Matcha tea can help improve memory and reduce stress and anxiety.",
    questionText: "Assume the market for matcha tea is in equilibrium (E1). Indicate, by means of a tick (✔), whether Diagram A or Diagram B shows its new market equilibrium position following media coverage of its positive health effects. Explain your answer including the effects on equilibrium price and equilibrium quantity.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"8 + 4","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Diagram A ✔", marks: 8, contextNote: "Tick DIAGRAM A, 8 marks: favourable media coverage changes tastes, so DEMAND shifts right to D2. Diagram B moves supply.\n\nIrish diagram labels: É1/É2 are demand curves, C1/C2 are equilibrium points; Praghas is price and Cainníocht is quantity. The scheme uses D/E instead. Select Léaráid A: demand shifts right and the new price and quantity are higher.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "• The demand curve shifts to the right (D2). • The demand for matcha tea will increase due to its health benefits being reported in the media, which increase consumers’ taste/preference for the drink. • The increase in demand will result in an excess demand or a shortage, which will drive up the new equilibrium price. • There will be a new higher equilibrium price. • There will be a new higher equilibrium quantity.", marks: 4, contextNote: "Explain, 4 marks: demand shifts right, the shortage at the old price drives the price up, and the new equilibrium price and quantity are both higher.", openList: true },
    ],
