    section: "A", questionRef: "2025 OL Section A Q4(a)",
    stem: "Budget 2025 comes with some great news for workers across Ireland, with the average worker set to save at least €1,000 - thanks to measures which included changes to the threshold of the higher tax bracket (allowing less income to be taxed at the higher rate of 40%), along with USC cuts and cost-of-living payments. Adapted from the Irish Independent",
    questionText: "Outline one reason why the government introduced the above measures.",
