    section: "B", questionRef: "2025 OL Q15(b)(ii)",
    stem: "It is forecasted that Ireland’s population will grow to 5.9 million by 2030. The diagram below shows the market demand curve and market supply curve for housing in Ireland. The forecasted increase in population is expected to affect the demand for housing. Show the effect of this development on the diagram above.",
    questionText: "Explain your answer.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"10","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "• The increase in population will lead to an increase in demand for housing as there will be more people willing and able to buy houses. • The demand curve will shift to the right (D to D1). • This will increase price to P1 • and Quantity will increase to Q1.", marks: 10, contextNote: "Explain the shift and its effect on price and quantity, 10 marks.", openList: true },
    ],
