    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2026 Ordinary Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2026-ol-q12-a-ii", topicId: "economics-2-0", conceptId: "ryanair-entry-and-passenger-numbers",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2026 OL Q12(a)(ii)",
    stem: "Aer Lingus had a successful advertising campaign for the Annual College American Football Classic held in Croke Park in August 2025.",
    questionText: "If Ryanair were to enter the market for transatlantic flights, explain how this development may affect the number of people flying to Ireland.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 10","answer":1,"ofParts":3,"perPart":10}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "An effect — any one", marks: 10, contextNote: "One developed explanation, 10 marks.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":10,"options":["Increased competition/Lower air fares - Increased competition between airlines would likely lead to lower ticket prices. As air travel becomes cheaper, it becomes more affordable for consumers, causing an increase in the number of people flying into Ireland.","Increased choice of routes and flight times - A new airline may introduce new routes or more frequent flights. Greater choice and convenience make travelling to Ireland more attractive, encouraging more people to fly into the country.","Improved service quality - To compete, airlines may improve service quality (e.g. better customer service or free wifi). Higher quality makes flying more appealing, leading to an increase in the number of passengers travelling to Ireland."]} },
    ],
