    section: "B", questionRef: "2026 OL Q13(b)(ii)",
    stem: "The Irish government is expected to have a budget surplus of €7 billion for 2026. As a result, there is pressure on the government to reduce taxes.",
    questionText: "Outline one economic argument against reducing taxes.",
