    stem: "On 1st January 2026, the Irish government introduced an auto‐enrolment pension scheme for employees, who do not have a private pension. This means that for every €3 an employee puts into their pension, €4 more will be added to it: €3 by their employer and €1 by the State.",
    questionText: "Outline one possible economic advantage to the employee or one possible economic disadvantage to the employer of this scheme. Ticked box: DISADVANTAGE TO THE EMPLOYER.",
